    {"instruction": "How do I write a compelling headline?", "response": "Writing compelling headlines:\n1. Use numbers: '7 Ways to...' or '12 Books for...'\n2. Ask a question: 'Want to Earn More in 2026?'\n3. Create urgency: 'Limited Time: 80% Off!'\n4. Promise a benefit: 'Master Excel in 30 Days'\n5. Use power words: 'Complete', 'Proven', 'Secret', 'Ultimate'\n6. Keep it short (5-8 words ideal)\n7. Be specific, not vague\n8. Address the reader directly ('You')\n9. A/B test different headlines\n10. Match the content (don't clickbait)\n\nGood: '12 Books That Take You From Zero to Job-Ready'\nBad: 'Some Books About Computers'"},
